{"path":"string/byte/memset","title":"std::memset","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>memset","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/byte/memset","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Copies the value static_cast<unsigned char>(ch) into each of the first count characters of the object pointed to by dest.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstring\">&lt;cstring&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> memset<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> dest, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> ch, <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Copies the value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>ch<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> into each of the first <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> characters of the object pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>. If the object is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/object#Subobjects\">potentially-overlapping subobject</a> or is not <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/TriviallyCopyable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">TriviallyCopyable</em></a> (e.g., scalar, C-compatible struct, or an array of trivially copyable type), the behavior is undefined. If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code> is greater than the size of the object pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>, the behavior is undefined.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> dest\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the object to fill\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ch\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> fill byte\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> count\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> number of bytes to fill\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">dest</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>std::memset</code> may be optimized away (under the <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/as_if\">as-if</a> rules) if the object modified by this function is not accessed again for the rest of its lifetime (e.g., <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=8537\" data-external=\"1\">gcc bug 8537</a>). For that reason, this function cannot be used to scrub memory (e.g., to fill an array that stored a password with zeroes).\n</p><p>Solutions for that include <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/fill\"><code>std::fill</code></a> with volatile pointers, <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c23\">(C23)</span> <a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/memset\"><code>memset_explicit()</code></a>, <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c11\">(C11)</span> <a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/memset\"><code>memset_s</code></a>, FreeBSD <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?query=explicit_bzero\" data-external=\"1\">explicit_bzero</a> or Microsoft <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/aa366877.aspx\" data-external=\"1\"><code>SecureZeroMemory</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;bitset&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;climits&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstring&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> a<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> bits <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/bitset\"><span class=\"kw1034\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bitset</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>sizeof<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/climits\"><span class=\"kw394\">CHAR_BIT</span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">memset</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a, <span class=\"nu6\">0b1111</span><span class=\"st0\">'0000'</span><span class=\"nu8\">0011</span>, sizeof a<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> ai <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> a<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> bits<span class=\"br0\">(</span>ai<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>00000011000000110000001100000011\n00000011000000110000001100000011\n00000011000000110000001100000011\n00000011000000110000001100000011</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/memcpy\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>memcpy</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copies one buffer to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/memmove\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>memmove</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  moves one buffer to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/wide/wmemset\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wmemset</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copies the given wide character to every position in a wide character array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/fill\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>fill</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copy-assigns the given value to every element in a range <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/fill_n\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>fill_n</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  copy-assigns the given value to N elements in a range <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_trivially_copyable\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_trivially_copyable</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type is trivially copyable  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/string/byte/memset\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>memset</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/byte","title":"Null-terminated byte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::memset","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Copies the value static_cast<unsigned char>(ch) into each of the first count characters of the object pointed to by…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"dest, ch, count"},{"label":"Return value","note":"dest"},{"label":"Notes","note":"std::memset may be optimized away (under the as-if rules) if the object modified by this function is not accessed again for the rest of its lifetime (e.g…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"memcpy","note":"copies one buffer to another"},{"label":"memmove","note":"moves one buffer to another"},{"label":"wmemset","note":"copies the given wide character to every position in a wide character array"},{"label":"fill","note":"copy-assigns the given value to every element in a range"},{"label":"fill_n","note":"copy-assigns the given value to N elements in a range"},{"label":"is_trivially_copyable","note":"checks if a type is trivially copyable"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":280,"codeBlockCount":2}
